+# blender-web (M2.3/M2.5): give the main `blender` executable the node-runnable
+# headless link profile. This runs AFTER setup_platform_linker_flags(blender) on
+# purpose: that macro APPENDS the global PLATFORM_LINKFLAGS (which carries
+# -sMALLOC=mimalloc, correct for the browser/gtest binaries) and mimalloc
+# duplicate-symbol-clashes with the mimalloc CPython 3.13 vendors inside
+# libpython3.13.a. blender_web_node_binary() (defined in patches/platform_wasm.cmake)
+# OVERWRITES LINK_FLAGS with a self-contained node profile using -sMALLOC=dlmalloc,
+# so it must be the LAST word on this target's link flags. No-op on native.
+if(EMSCRIPTEN)
+  blender_web_node_binary(blender)
+endif()
+
